+because Z_A has no original coefficient sources. For RD3's specified
+two-block history this derivative is strictly negative also at sufficiently
+distant original plaquettes p. To verify the positivity premise directly,
+put one interior g mark at coordinates (1,1,1,1) in each of its two
+adjacent blocks, and identity elsewhere. With cut one, only those blocks
+are bad; their size two exceeds the history's size-success threshold one,
+independently of U_1. Link perturbations smaller than 1/16 change every
+plaquette by less than 1/4 and preserve that complete failure list.
+On a distant plaquette perturb one unmarked link to
+diag(exp(i theta),exp(-i theta),1,...,1) for a sufficiently small nonzero
+theta. Then s_p=2(1-cos theta)/N>0, and an open subcap retains this strict
+inequality and the history. Positive kernels give positive mass to that
+subcap at every fixed real V, proving the strict sign in (A23b).
+
